Using the LHCb data collected at 13 TeV, we studied the charmless b to d transitions involving tau leptons and their corresponding neutrinos. Specifically, we examined four decay modes: $B^0	o D^{*0}	au^- ar{
u}_	au$, $B^0	o D^0	au^- ar{
u}_	au$, $B^+	o D^*	au^- ar{
u}_	au$, and $B^+	o D^+	au^- ar{
u}_	au$. By comparing the branching fractions of these tau decays to those of $B	o D^{(*)}\ell^- ar{
u}_\ell$ decays with electrons or muons, we found the ratios to be within the range of 0.6 to 1.4, with a 95% confidence interval.
